# Bench runs are never committed - none of it, not even with `add -f`.
# A run directory is raw instrument output: the .csv rows (tens of thousands
# per long hold), console.log byte-for-byte, meta.json and status.json. It is
# INPUT to the figure scripts in docs/environment/figures/, not a record
# anyone reads. A result that matters goes into a figure and into
# PROJECT_CONTEXT_WHEEL_FW.md; the data behind it stays on the bench machine.
# Regenerating a figure therefore needs the run directory locally, which is
# the trade: repo size over one-command reproduction.
runs/

# Belt and braces, in case a run lands outside runs/.
*.csv
*.log

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
